{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\178.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "We can find perpendicular", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[261, 172], [680, 161], [681, 201], [262, 212]]}, {"text": "lines in real-life objects.", "conf": 0.893, "box": [[261, 224], [634, 215], [635, 251], [262, 260]]}, {"text": "9.2.3 Angles", "conf": 0.836, "box": [[101, 857], [346, 855], [346, 898], [102, 900]]}, {"text": "We have already learnt about different types of lines, line", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[102, 917], [1038, 907], [1039, 947], [103, 957]]}, {"text": "segments, angles and triangles.", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[102, 969], [608, 965], [609, 1004], [102, 1008]]}, {"text": "Look at thefigures.We can identifythat thesefigures are", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[104, 1020], [1045, 1018], [1045, 1054], [104, 1056]]}, {"text": "made up of different types of lines and angles.", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[98, 1071], [862, 1073], [862, 1109], [98, 1106]]}, {"text": "An angle is formed when two lines intersect each other.", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[105, 1122], [1019, 1122], [1019, 1158], [105, 1158]]}, {"text": "Look at the figure OA and OB are two rays that meet at a", "conf": 0.916, "box": [[98, 1158], [1052, 1166], [1051, 1221], [97, 1214]]}, {"text": "point to make an angle AOB or ZO. Two rays A and OB", "conf": 0.934, "box": [[101, 1222], [1042, 1216], [1043, 1269], [101, 1275]]}, {"text": "are called the arms of the angle AOB. Let's learn about", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[104, 1275], [1007, 1285], [1006, 1324], [103, 1314]]}, {"text": "some more concepts related to angles.", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[101, 1330], [745, 1337], [744, 1376], [100, 1369]]}, {"text": "Adjacent Angles", "conf": 0.829, "box": [[107, 1438], [437, 1444], [436, 1488], [106, 1482]]}, {"text": "Two angles are said to be adjacent to each other if they fulfil the following conditions:", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[106, 1491], [1571, 1515], [1570, 1557], [105, 1533]]}, {"text": "i) They have a common vertex.", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[107, 1545], [628, 1558], [627, 1598], [106, 1585]]}, {"text": "ii) They have a common arm.", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[108, 1600], [599, 1612], [598, 1652], [107, 1639]]}, {"text": "ili) They lie on the opposite side of the common arm (i.e. they do not overlap)", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[107, 1651], [1415, 1681], [1414, 1724], [106, 1694]]}, {"text": "Look at the figure.", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[106, 1705], [410, 1717], [409, 1757], [105, 1745]]}, {"text": "ZAOC and ZAOB are adjacent angles as:", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[111, 1761], [785, 1778], [784, 1820], [110, 1803]]}, {"text": ". They have a common vertex O.", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[132, 1817], [692, 1831], [691, 1874], [131, 1860]]}, {"text": "They have a common arm A.", "conf": 0.863, "box": [[150, 1873], [676, 1873], [676, 1923], [150, 1923]]}, {"text": " They lie on the opposite side of the common arm and", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[169, 1928], [1084, 1949], [1083, 1992], [168, 1971]]}, {"text": "are not overlapping.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[174, 1981], [512, 1995], [510, 2039], [172, 2025]]}, {"text": "176", "conf": 0.74, "box": [[812, 2114], [888, 2114], [888, 2154], [812, 2154]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[1215, 2132], [1537, 2142], [1536, 2178], [1213, 2168]]}]}